Package: pmbfa
Type: Package
Title: Parsimonious Mixtures of Bilinear Factor Analyzers
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R: person("Jacob", "Moore", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "jacob.c.moore55@gmail.com")
Description: Fits parsimonious mixtures of normal and skewed matrix-variate
    bilinear factor analyzers using an alternating expectation conditional
    maximization algorithm. Provides constrained covariance models, shared
    initialization, adaptive constraint selection, and factor searches for
    normal, skew-t, generalized hyperbolic, normal inverse Gaussian, and
    variance-gamma component distributions. Numerical fitting and initialization
    use compiled C++ while model selection remains in R. Returned fits record
    original calls, elapsed wall-clock time, convergence and numerical diagnostics.
License: GPL (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/jacobmoore55/pmbfa
BugReports: https://github.com/jacobmoore55/pmbfa/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.1.0), stats, utils, parallel
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: C++17
NeedsCompilation: yes
